<quiz>
<question type="stack">
  <name><text>Finding an unknown from a coefficient</text></name>
  <questiontext format="html">
    <text><![CDATA[<p>In the expansion of \((1 + kx)^{@n@}\), where \(k\) is a positive number, the coefficient of \(x^{@r@}\) is \({@c@}\). Find \(k\).</p><div>\(k =\) [[input:ans1]] [[validation:ans1]] [[feedback:prt1]]</div>]]></text>
  </questiontext>
  <generalfeedback format="html">
    <text><![CDATA[<p>Number \({@r@}\) of the row for power \({@n@}\) is \({@C@}\), so the term in \(x^{@r@}\) is \({@C@}(kx)^{@r@} = {@C@}k^{@r@}x^{@r@}\).</p><p>\[{@C@}k^{@r@} = {@c@} \quad\Rightarrow\quad k^{@r@} = {@nopow@} \quad\Rightarrow\quad k = {@k@}\]</p>[[if test="is(r=2)"]]<p>The square root could also be \({@-k@}\), but \(k\) is positive, so \(k = {@kd@}\).</p>[[else]]<p>So \(k = {@kd@}\).</p>[[/if]]]]></text>
  </generalfeedback>
  <defaultgrade>1</defaultgrade>
  <penalty>0.1</penalty>
  <hidden>0</hidden>
  <idnumber></idnumber>
  <stackversion><text>2026063000</text></stackversion>
  <questionvariables>
    <text><![CDATA[/* Design: find one unknown from a condition on a coefficient. Source: adapted from SMP AS/A2 Core 2, Chapter 5, Exercise C, question 7. */
L: [[6,2,4],[8,3,2],[8,2,1/2],[5,3,4],[7,2,2],[10,3,1/2],[9,2,3],[6,3,3],[10,2,2],[9,2,1/2]];
ix: 1+rand(10);
n: L[ix][1];
r: L[ix][2];
k: L[ix][3];
C: binomial(n,r);
c: C*k^r;
nopow: c/C;
wrongC: float((c/n)^(1/r));
rootw: if r=2 then "square" else "cube";
kd: if k=1/2 then "0.5" else string(k);]]></text>
  </questionvariables>
