  <questiondescription format="html"><text><![CDATA[<p id="concept">Binomial Expansions: unknown from a coefficient</p><p id="description">Grade 12 CBE Core 1.2: Find a positive k from the coefficient of x^r in (1 + kx)^n.</p><p id="edition">Core</p><p id="provenance">This question is adapted from Chapter 5, Section C, Exercise C, question 7 of Cassell, D., Instone, S., Ling, J., Scruton, P., Shilton, S. and West, H., SMP AS/A2 Mathematics: Core 2 for AQA, Cambridge University Press, 2004: reduced to one unknown in a bracket (1 + kx)^n with a given coefficient, new numbers, randomised.</p><p id="citation">INNODEMS CBC Grade 12 Mathematics, first draft by Ben Davies, 2026. Aligned to the KICD Senior School Curriculum Design, Core Mathematics Grade 12 (draft).</p>]]></text></questiondescription>
